<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ Food Price Index falls 0.8 pct in May.</title>
<headline>NZ Food Price Index falls 0.8 pct in May.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand on Friday released the following data for the Food Price Index for May:</p>
<p>     May 1997	     Apr 1997	   May 1996</p>
<p>    -0.8 pct	     +0.1 pct	   +0.8 pct</p>
<p>yr-end May 1997  yr-end Apr 1997  yr-end May 1996</p>
<p>    +1.7 pct	     +3.4 pct	    0.0 pct</p>
<p>Note - The index makes up 18 percent of the consumer price index (CPI).  </p>
<p>Food subgroups:</p>
<p>percentage change from the same month of the previous year:</p>
<p>				    May 1997</p>
<p>    Fruit and Vegetables    +1.6 pct</p>
<p>    Meat, fish and poultry  +2.7 pct</p>
<p>    Grocery food etc	  +1.6 pct</p>
<p>    Restaurants		 +1.5 pct</p>
<p>percentage change from previous month:</p>
<p>    Fruit and Vegetables    -7.1 pct</p>
<p>    Meat, fish and poultry  +1.2 pct</p>
<p>    Grocery food etc	  no change</p>
<p>    Restaurants		 -0.1 pct</p>
<p>--Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
